; ======================================================================
;  THE TEMPERATURE - NOT A CAPABILITY, AND NOT KNOWN.
;
;  HwTemp* has no #CAP_ flag: the core takes a reading once a second at
;  the prompt whether or not a fan is armed, and a board that cannot
;  answer says so with #HW_TEMP_NONE rather than by being absent.
;
;  THE SENSOR EXISTS. The BCM2837 has an on-die thermal sensor and the
;  firmware will report it through the property mailbox. This monitor
;  does not ask, for the reason every mailbox question on this board runs
;  into: the mailbox stops answering once the MMU is on, and a
;  once-a-second reading is exactly the kind of thing that cannot be
;  asked during boot and remembered. Reading the sensor's own registers
;  is the answer, and it is work nobody has done here.
;
;  SO IT ANSWERS UNKNOWN AND THE ROW SAYS UNKNOWN. A plausible constant
;  would be the worst possible value in a field whose whole purpose is to
;  tell somebody their board is hot.
; ======================================================================

Procedure.i HwTempMaxMilliC()
  ProcedureReturn #HW_TEMP_NONE
EndProcedure
Procedure.i HwTempMilliC()
  ProcedureReturn #HW_TEMP_NONE
EndProcedure
Procedure.i HwTempSource()
  ProcedureReturn #HW_TEMP_SRC_NONE
EndProcedure

